{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015UpNfKrEJ6RfNhVAhcpk2w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"worst\" tier scenario. Let me carefully go through the worst tier definition:\n\n**Worst tier meaning**: NVE threshold classification fails OR Cheetah control doesn't replicate; core causal chain questioned; needs full reframe but not venue downgrade.\n\n**Core assumptions for worst**:\n- Cheetah control experiment NVE > 2.0× (cross-environment causal control fails — high NVE even without dt_emb)\n- 008f_s3 NVE > 1.5× (untrained dt_emb protection falsified at third seed)\n\n\n- NVE 1.5× threshold classifier drops below 75% accuracy, introducing false positives and negatives that undermine the classification narrative\n- Reviewers push back on the scope being too narrow with only Walker Walk and DreamerV3 as clean cases for a CoRL venue\n- The 35pp decomposition gets rejected because 018v2's 51% residual degradation remains unexplained and potentially confounded with SGS side effects\n- The dual-pathway explanation reads as post-hoc rather than a genuine mechanistic insight\n\nNow I'm looking at the metric ranges that define this worst-case scenario.\n\nThe core causal chain—where trained dt_emb leads to CIVO and then collapse—doesn't generalize as a universal mechanism, suggesting it might be specific to Walker Walk and RSSM architectures instead. I should reframe this toward a methodology or architecture-level contribution rather than a broad causal claim. Now I'm going through the planned experiments to generate predicted results under this pessimistic scenario, starting with plan_011 on Walker Walk.\n\nLooking at the remaining planned experiments: several Walker Walk variants with different seeds, Cheetah Run experiments testing dt_emb with various configurations, and analyses of