n_013, I'm considering how additional seeds might expose brittleness in the baseline approach.\n\nDrafting this up in YAML format now... For plan_021, I already have the CIVO trigger result showing massive NVE spike, but worst-case runs would show lower peaks that blur the distinction from baseline. Plan_022 is the critical one—dt_embed_dim=0 on Cheetah produces NVE in the 2-5× range, which breaks the causal story I'm building across environments. Plans_023 and 030 both risk muddying the narrative: untrained embeddings show elevated NVE without clear protection, and Cheetah's RSSM fidelity pattern diverges from Walker's, weakening the mechanistic explanation. Plan_034 on threshold sensitivity is still incomplete.\n\nFor plan_034, the worst case is AUROC dropping below 0.85 with threshold shifts across environments and classification accuracy stuck under 75%. Cartpole (plans_050-052) replicates the same problem as Cheetah—no clean separation. Hopper gives mixed results, and the uncertainty truncation pilot either fails to help or introduces new failure modes. I need to consolidate all this into a structured YAML with metrics and failure rationales.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41760,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41760},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f272e0bb-5347-482e-afcd-36240c7eec89","uuid":"37f9efa2-6fb9-44db-8182-b75221e4d08a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015UpNfKrEJ6RfNhVAhcpk2w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心因果链（trained dt_emb → CIVO → collapse）作为 universal mechanism 不成立——\n  可能是 Walker Walk + RSSM 的特异性现象，而非 imagination-based AC 的通用漏洞。\n  Reframe 方向（仍冲 CoRL）：从 \"mechanism paper\" 转为 \"methodology paper\"——\n  贡献不是 CIVO 本身，而是 factorial diagnosis + NVE monitoring + gradient decomposition 的诊断方法论。\n  关键失败点：Cheetah 控制实验 NVE > 2.0×（跨环境因果控制失败）；008f_s3 NVE > 1.5×（untrained dt_emb 保护被否证）；\n  NVE 1.5× 阈值分类精度 < 75%。35pp decomposition 被 confound with SGS side effects。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse with 2 more seeds (009e seed 1, 009b seed 2)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 55000\n      seed1_eval_final_105K: 131\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 25000\n      seed2_eval_final_105K: 268\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      collapse_rate: 0.5\n      nve_exceeds_1_5x_rate: 1.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据（009e collapsed NVE 4.12×@55K; 009b self-corrected NVE 2.05×→0.38×）。\n      在 worst 档，这些结果本身成立，但 1/2 崩溃率意味着 CIVO 不是确定性的——\n      仅是一个随机事件。当 Cheetah 的 dt_embed_dim=0 控制也出现 NVE>2.0× 时，\n      Walker Walk 的 1/2 崩溃率变得不具说服力：究竟是 trained dt_emb 引起的，\n      还是配置组合的随机脆弱性？审稿人将质疑 n=2 的统计功效。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008d cross-seed comparison\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, nve_peak_step, eval_105K, collapse, mechanism]\n        rows:\n          - [0(=009e), 4.12, 55K, 131, yes, \"value-driven CIVO\"]\n          - [2(=009b), 2.05, 25K, 268, no, \"transient→self-correction\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectory overlay: seed 0 accelerating to 4.12× vs seed 2 transient spike then monotone decline\"\n    analysis: >\n      崩溃率 50% 在 worst 档下不足以支持 mechanism claim——reviewer 会说这是 \"coin flip\"\n      而非 \"reliable trigger\"。NVE>1.5× threshold 在 Walker Walk 内部仍有 4/4 separation，\n      但当 Cheetah 控制实验也出现高 NVE 时，这个 threshold 的跨环境泛化性崩溃。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control stability — 008f_s3 (third seed) 是关键\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009f_status: killed_no_data\n      seed2_009c_eval_105K: 148.34\n      seed2_009c_nve_105K: 1.14\n      seed3_008f_s3_eval_peak: 280\n      seed3_008f_s3_eval_105K: 165\n      seed3_008f_s3_nve_peak: 1.72\n      seed3_008f_s3_nve_peak_step: 85000\n      seed3_exceeds_1_5x: true\n      protection_falsified: true\n      classification_accuracy_post_s3: 0.71\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：008f_s3 NVE > 1.5×。机制：在 dt_embed_dim=0 条件下，\n      RSSM 仍需处理 dt=2 transitions（subsample ON），reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2\n      （reward gap 1.01×），但 observation decoder 的 dt=2 误差累积在某些 seed 下\n      仍可通过 critic 误导 actor。009c 已在 105K 达到 NVE=1.14×（borderline），\n      008f_s3 在更长 run 或不同初始化下跨越 1.5×。这不是经典 CIVO（无 dt_emb amplification），\n      而是 \"raw RSSM fidelity gap\" 本身的有限 value overestimation——但它破坏了\n      NVE 1.5× 作为 trained vs untrained dt_emb 的 perfect separator 的故事。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008f (no dt_emb) all seeds NVE summary\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, nve_peak_step, exceeds_1.5x, eval_105K]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 1.02, 25K, no, 503]\n          - [2(009c), 1.14, 105K, no, 148]\n          - [3(008f_s3), 1.72, 85K, \"YES\", 165]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectory: three 008f seeds overlaid, with 1.5× threshold line — s3 crosses threshold\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f_s3 跨越 NVE 1.5× 是 worst 档的核心打击点。此前 4/4 perfect separation\n      （trained 2/2 exceed, untrained 0/2 exceed）变为 5/7 imperfect separation\n      （trained 2/2+009e+009b=4/4 exceed, untrained 1/3 exceed = 008f_s3）。\n      分类精度从 100% 降至 ~71%（5/7 correct）。审稿人将质疑：如果没有 dt_emb\n      也能出现 NVE>1.5×，那么 trained dt_emb 真的是 \"necessary condition\" 吗？\n      或仅是 \"amplifier\"？这削弱了整个 C2 因果链从 \"necessary and sufficient\" 到 \"risk factor\"。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination mitigation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 869.9\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 137.0\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_mechanism: eval_driven_not_CIVO\n      collapse_rate: 0.5\n      mitigation_reliability: unreliable\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据确认（s1 成功 95% baseline, s2 崩溃 via non-CIVO pathway）。\n      在 worst 档，这个 50% 崩溃率与 008d 的 50% 完全相同——dt=1 imagination\n      作为 mitigation 零效果。更糟的是 s2 的崩溃机制（eval-driven, entropy ↑）\n      与经典 CIVO 不同，被 reviewer 视为 \"ad hoc dual-pathway explanation\"\n      而非 genuine insight。审稿人评价：\"claiming two distinct pathways from n=2\n      per pathway is unfalsifiable post-hoc rationalization.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 cross-seed collapse comparison\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, nve_105K, collapse, pathway, entropy_direction]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 869.9, 0.80, no, \"-\", stable]\n          - [2, 137.0, 3.78, yes, \"Pathway B (eval-driven)\", \"↑ -5.21→-3.83\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-panel: s1 healthy monotone rise vs s2 late-onset collapse with diverging entropy\"\n    analysis: >\n      Dual-pathway 在 worst 档被视为 ad hoc。Reviewer 核心批评：\n      \"Two pathways from two seeds is curve-fitting, not science. Show me 10 seeds\n      with clear bimodal distribution, or this is just noise.\" 50% collapse rate\n      means dt=1 imagination provides zero marginal safety over dt=2 imagination\n      (008d also 50%). The entire C6 story collapses into \"trained dt_emb is bad,\n      and we have no mitigation.\"\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 520\n      seed1_nve_range: [0.55, 0.95]\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_recovery_pattern: single_dip_recovery\n      seed2_eval_105K: 380\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.35\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 75000\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_pattern: slow_decline_after_peak\n      cross_seed_consistency: moderate\n      vs_baseline_mean: -48%\n    result_rationale: >\n      008a 的 \"untrained dt_emb\" 实际是 trained dt_emb unexposed to dt>1 data\n      （subsample OFF = 所有训练数据都是 dt=1）。在 worst 档，seed 间变异大：\n      seed 0 达到 778（85% baseline），但 seed 1/2 可能仅达到 380-520（40-57% baseline）。\n      V-recovery pattern 不稳定复现——有的 seed 单次 dip，有的缓慢下滑。\n      NVE 保持 <1.5× 但绝对性能远低于 baseline，reviewer 质疑：\n      \"suppressed v/e is not suppressed degradation — 008a still loses 48% performance,\n      making it useless as mitigation.\" 这削弱了 C3 从 \"protection\" 到 \"delayed failure\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008a cross-seed summary\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, vs_baseline_pct, nve_peak, collapse, pattern]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 778, \"-15%\", 0.93, no, \"zigzag recovery\"]\n          - [1, 520, \"-43%\", 0.95, no, \"single dip recovery\"]\n          - [2, 380, \"-59%\", 1.35, no, \"slow decline post-peak\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-seed 008a eval curves showing high inter-seed variance; all below baseline but no collapse\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 核心 claim 是 \"untrained dt_emb prevents optimistic drift\" — 这在 worst 档仍成立\n      （NVE < 1.5×），但 practical value 被质疑。平均 -48% vs baseline 意味着\n      \"preventing collapse by preventing learning\" — reviewer 评价：\n      \"You've shown that removing information prevents exploitation, which is trivially true.\"\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"Frozen dt_embedding (requires_grad=False), 诊断 dt_emb TRAINING 是否是必要条件\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 204\n      nve_peak: 0.47\n      nve_105K: 0.42\n      collapse: false\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      mechanism: gradient_starvation\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      comparison_vs_008d: \"no collapse but severe underperformance\"\n      comparison_vs_008f: \"similar non-collapse but different mechanism\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 exp_015b 数据：NVE 0.39-0.47（远低于 1.0，critic 低估），actor_loss→0\n      （gradient starvation），eval 80-238 高波动无稳定收敛。在 worst 档，\n      这个结果被 reviewer 视为 confounding：frozen dt_emb 不崩溃是因为\n      gradient starvation 阻止了所有学习，不是因为 dt_emb training 是 CIVO 的原因。\n      \"You prevented CIVO by preventing learning entirely — this doesn't isolate the mechanism.\"\n      与 008f（dt_embed_dim=0）的区别不清晰：两者都不崩溃，但原因可能完全不同\n      （015b = gradient starvation; 008f = no conditioning information）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Frozen dt_emb vs controls\"\n        columns: [config, eval_105K, nve_peak, mechanism, informative_for_C2]\n        rows:\n          - [\"015b (frozen)\", 204, 0.47, \"gradient starvation\", \"confounded\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained)\", 131, 4.12, \"CIVO\", \"yes (positive control)\"]\n          - [\"008f (dim=0)\", 503, 1.02, \"no conditioning\", \"yes (negative control)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-way comparison: 008d collapse, 008f zigzag recovery, 015b flat low-performance\"\n    analysis: >\n      015b 在 worst 档被视为 uninformative control。Reviewer 评价：\n      \"Freezing the embedding creates a fundamentally different learning regime\n      (gradient starvation in actor) — you cannot conclude that training is the\n      causal factor when your intervention has multiple confounded effects.\"\n      2×2 消融矩阵（trained/frozen × exposed/unexposed）的 frozen row 全部被\n      gradient starvation 污染，无法干净解读。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Narrow true collapse probability of dt=1 imagination config\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_105K: 780\n      seed3_nve_105K: 0.72\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      seed4_eval_105K: 95\n      seed4_nve_peak: 4.2\n      seed4_nve_peak_step: 85000\n      seed4_collapse: true\n      seed4_mechanism: \"mixed — value and eval co-decline\"\n      total_collapse_rate: \"2/4 = 50%\"\n      confidence_interval_collapse_rate: \"[0.15, 0.85] (Clopper-Pearson 95%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下，008e_v3 的崩溃率维持 ~50%（2/4 seeds collapse）。Seed 4 崩溃\n      机制既不完全像 Pathway A（value explosion）也不完全像 Pathway B（eval-driven），\n      而是 \"mixed\" — 进一步削弱 dual-pathway 作为干净分类的可信度。\n      Clopper-Pearson 95% CI for 2/4 = [0.07, 0.93]，统计功效极低。\n      Reviewer 评价：\"50% collapse from n=4 gives CI [0.07, 0.93] — you literally\n      cannot distinguish this from any collapse rate between 7% and 93%.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 all seeds summary\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, nve_105K, collapse, mechanism_classification]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 869.9, 0.80, no, healthy]\n          - [2, 137.0, 3.78, yes, \"Pathway B (eval-driven)\"]\n          - [3, 780, 0.72, no, healthy]\n          - [4, 95, 4.2, yes, \"mixed/ambiguous\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Four-seed overlay showing bimodal outcome: 2 converge ~800+, 2 collapse <150\"\n    analysis: >\n      50% collapse rate with wide CI is statistically uninformative. The existence of\n      a third mechanism pattern (seed 4 \"mixed\") destroys the dual-pathway narrative.\n      Reviewer 核心批评：\"每多一个 seed 就发明一条新 pathway — 这不是 mechanism discovery，\n      是 overfitting to noise.\" CoRL 审稿标准要求 reproducible results，50% collapse\n      from a supposedly safe configuration is unacceptable for a practical recommendation.\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_peak: 850\n      seed0_eval_500K: 820\n      seed1_eval_peak: 790\n      seed1_eval_500K: 760\n      seed2_eval_peak: 810\n      seed2_eval_500K: 780\n      mean_eval_500K: 787\n      std_eval_500K: 30\n      ve_stable_range: \"0.65-0.75\"\n      baseline_established: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Baseline 在任何 tier 下都应成功——这是 vanilla DreamerV3 on Cheetah Run。\n      已有 exp_010a 达到 849.8。Worst 档下 baseline 正常，cross-seed 一致性好，\n      建立了干净的 reference。这不是 failure point；failure 在后续实验。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah baseline 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_peak, eval_500K, ve_stable]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 850, 820, 0.71]\n          - [1, 790, 760, 0.68]\n          - [2, 810, 780, 0.73]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-seed Cheetah baseline learning curves — consistent convergence to 760-820 range\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 正常建立。为后续 CIVO trigger 和 causal control 提供 reference。\n      Cross-seed std ~30 (3.8% of mean) 表明 Cheetah 的 seed sensitivity 低于 Walker Walk。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO collapse in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_nve_peak: 8.5\n      seed0_nve_peak_step: 75000\n      seed0_collapse: true\n      seed0_eval_105K: 85\n      seed1_nve_peak: 5.2\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 65000\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_eval_105K: 120\n      seed2_nve_peak: 3.8\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 55000\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 310\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      collapse_rate: \"2/3\"\n      mean_nve_peak: 5.83\n      cross_env_replication: partial\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 exp_010b 达到 NVE 14.59× 并崩溃。Worst 档下 CIVO trigger 仍部分成功\n      （2/3 collapse），但 peak NVE 范围 3.8-8.5×（低于 Walker Walk 的 009e 4.12×\n      仅作为下限）。关键问题不在 trigger（它 works），而在 control 不 work。\n      NVE 仍 >1.5× in all seeds，确认 trained dt_emb 确实 triggers pathological overestimation。\n      但 severity 和 timing 跨环境不一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah CIVO trigger 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, peak_step, eval_105K, collapse, vs_baseline_105K]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 8.5, 75K, 85, yes, \"-89%\"]\n          - [1, 5.2, 65K, 120, yes, \"-85%\"]\n          - [2, 3.8, 55K, 310, no, \"-60%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectories for 3 Cheetah CIVO seeds, with Walker Walk 008d/009b overlay for comparison\"\n    analysis: >\n      CIVO trigger 在 Cheetah 仍触发高 NVE，但 timing 和 severity 不同于 Walker Walk。\n      这本身不是 worst 档的核心问题——问题在于 control 也出现高 NVE。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"核心跨环境因果控制 — worst 档的关键失败点\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_nve_peak: 2.8\n      seed0_nve_peak_step: 75000\n      seed0_eval_105K: 280\n      seed0_exceeds_1_5x: true\n      seed1_nve_peak: 2.1\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 85000\n      seed1_eval_105K: 350\n      seed1_exceeds_1_5x: true\n      seed2_nve_peak: 3.5\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 65000\n      seed2_eval_105K: 190\n      seed2_exceeds_1_5x: true\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      mean_nve_peak: 2.8\n      all_exceed_1_5x: true\n      causal_control_failed: true\n      cheetah_control_nve_peak: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 worst 档的核心破坏性结果。Cheetah 中去掉 dt_embedding 后 NVE 仍达 2.0-3.5×。\n      机制解释：Cheetah Run 的 reward landscape 比 Walker Walk 更稀疏（locomotion reward\n      与速度线性相关，但 early training 中 reward signal 噪声大），RSSM 在 Cheetah 中\n      即使没有 dt_emb conditioning，dt=2 transitions 的 reward prediction 偏差也足够\n      大，能通过 critic 产生显著 value overestimation。具体来说，Cheetah 的 reward_MAE\n      at dt=2 即使无 dt_emb 也达到 baseline 的 3-5×（不像 Walker Walk 的 008f 的 75×\n      那么极端，但方向相同且 impact 不同）。这意味着 \"dt_embedding is necessary for CIVO\"\n      仅在 Walker Walk 成立——在 Cheetah 中，RSSM fidelity gap at dt=2 本身就足以\n      trigger pathological overestimation without dt_emb amplification。因果链从\n      \"trained dt_emb → CIVO\" 变为 \"RSSM dt=2 error → CIVO（dt_emb amplifies but\n      is not necessary）\"。这是对 C2 核心 claim 的根本否证。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah dt_embed_dim=0 — CONTROL FAILED\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, peak_step, eval_105K, exceeds_1.5x, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 2.8, 75K, 280, \"YES\", no]\n          - [1, 2.1, 85K, 350, \"YES\", no]\n          - [2, 3.5, 65K, 190, \"YES\", yes]\n      - title: \"Cross-environment causal control comparison\"\n        columns: [environment, config, seeds_exceeding_1.5x, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"0/3\", \"control holds\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"no dt_emb\", \"3/3\", \"CONTROL FAILS\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"008d (trained dt_emb)\", \"2/2\", \"CIVO confirmed\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"trained dt_emb\", \"3/3\", \"CIVO confirmed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment NVE comparison: Walker 008f (all <1.5×) vs Cheetah no-dt-emb (all >1.5×)\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: dt_embed_dim=0 NVE vs environment, showing environment-specific behavior\"\n    analysis: >\n      核心灾难：在 Cheetah 中，去掉 dt_embedding 不能阻止 NVE>1.5×。\n      这直接否证了 \"trained dt_emb is necessary for CIVO\" 作为跨环境通用规律。\n      可能的解释：Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 本身更大（不需要 dt_emb 放大），\n      或者 Cheetah 的 reward structure 让 critic 更容易被 dt=2 误差误导。\n      无论哪种解释，都意味着 Walker Walk 的干净 4/4 separation 是 environment-specific artifact。\n      NVE 1.5× threshold 不是 universal diagnostic marker for trained dt_emb —\n      它是 \"RSSM fidelity sufficient for critic exploitation\" 的 marker，\n      而 dt_emb 仅在某些环境中是该条件的必要 amplifier。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 450\n      seed0_nve_peak: 1.6\n      seed0_nve_105K: 1.2\n      seed1_eval_105K: 520\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.4\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.9\n      seed2_eval_105K: 380\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.8\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.5\n      mean_eval_105K: 450\n      vs_baseline_mean: \"-43%\"\n      seeds_exceeding_1_5x: \"2/3\"\n      protection_partial: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah 中仅提供部分保护。\n      由于 Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 更大（见 plan_022 rationale），\n      即使 dt_emb 未暴露于 dt>1 数据，RSSM 本身在处理环境动态时\n      产生的 compounding error 也会推高 value estimates。2/3 seeds 的 NVE\n      触及或超过 1.5×（虽然短暂），与 Walker Walk 008a 的 consistently <1.0×\n      形成鲜明对比。C3 的 \"untrained dt_emb prevents optimistic drift\"\n      在 Cheetah 中不成立 — 再次说明现象的 environment-specificity。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb (no subsample) 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, nve_peak, nve_105K, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 450, 1.6, 1.2, \"-43%\"]\n          - [1, 520, 1.4, 0.9, \"-34%\"]\n          - [2, 380, 1.8, 1.5, \"-52%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 008a-equivalent vs Walker 008a: NVE trajectories showing environment-dependent suppression\"\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst 档，C3 的 value growth suppression 仅在 Walker Walk 干净复现。\n      Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 的保护力度显著减弱。这进一步支持\n      \"Walker Walk + RSSM 特异性\" 叙事 — CIVO 和 anti-CIVO 机制\n      都是 environment-specific 的，没有 universal pattern。\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1\"\n    expected_results:\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_gap: 3.2\n      cheetah_baseline_reward_gap: 2.8\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_obs_gap: 3.8\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_reward_gap: 1.8\n      cheetah_trained_dt_emb_obs_gap: 1.5\n      cheetah_trained_dt_emb_reward_gap: 3.9\n      walker_vs_cheetah_fidelity_pattern: inconsistent\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity pattern 与 Walker Walk 不同。关键差异：\n      (1) Cheetah baseline obs gap (3.2×) > Walker baseline (2.04×) — Cheetah 的\n      RSSM 在 dt=2 预测本身就更差。(2) Cheetah no_dt_emb reward_gap (1.8×)\n      远高于 Walker 008f (1.01×) — 即使没有 dt_emb，Cheetah 的 reward 预测\n      在 dt=2 时仍有显著偏差。这解释了 plan_022 的失败：Walker 008f 的 reward\n      gap 接近 1.0 使 critic 不被误导，但 Cheetah 的 1.8× reward gap 足以\n      trigger value overestimation without dt_emb。RSSM fidelity analysis 揭示\n      核心问题不是 dt_emb training per se，而是 RSSM dt=2 reward prediction quality —\n      dt_emb 仅在 reward gap 本身低时才是关键 amplifier。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment RSSM fidelity comparison\"\n        columns: [env, config, obs_gap, reward_gap, NVE_outcome]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker, baseline, 2.04, 1.56, healthy]\n          - [Walker, \"008d (trained dt_emb)\", 1.30, 2.78, \"CIVO collapse\"]\n          - [Walker, \"008f (no dt_emb)\", 2.75, 1.01, \"no collapse\"]\n          - [Cheetah, baseline, 3.2, 2.8, healthy]\n          - [Cheetah, \"trained dt_emb\", 1.5, 3.9, \"CIVO collapse\"]\n          - [Cheetah, \"no dt_emb\", 3.8, 1.8, \"NVE>2.0× (!)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: reward_gap × obs_gap × collapse outcome, colored by environment\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSSM fidelity analysis 在 worst 档下揭示一个关键 insight：\n      CIVO 的 necessary condition 不是 trained dt_emb，而是 \"sufficient reward\n      prediction error at dt>1 to mislead critic\"。dt_emb 在 Walker Walk 中是\n      这个条件的 sole enabler（008f reward_gap=1.01 without dt_emb），但在 Cheetah\n      中 RSSM 本身的 dt=2 reward error 就足够大（1.8× without dt_emb）。\n      这是 important methodological finding 但破坏了 C2 的 clean causal story。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor_entropy vs training step for healthy vs collapsed configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_entropy_decline_rate: -0.035_per_1K_steps\n      walker_008e_v3_s2_entropy_rise_rate: +0.028_per_1K_steps\n      cheetah_collapsed_entropy_pattern: mixed\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_collapsed_seed2_entropy: declining\n      pathway_classification_consistency: poor\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy analysis 在 worst 档下进一步混淆 mechanism classification。\n      Walker Walk 有干净的双模式（008d: entropy ↓ = CIVO Pathway A; 008e_v3_s2:\n      entropy ↑ = Pathway B）。但 Cheetah 的 collapsed seeds 不 fit 任何一种模式：\n      有的 entropy declining（像 Pathway A），有的 flat（neither A nor B），\n      有的 oscillating。这使得 \"dual-pathway\" framework 不能泛化到 Cheetah，\n      变成 Walker-Walk-specific phenomenology。审稿人评价：\n      \"The pathway taxonomy is descriptive, not predictive.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Entropy trajectory classification across environments\"\n        columns: [exp, env, collapse, entropy_direction, pathway_assignment]\n        rows:\n          - [008d_s0, Walker, yes, \"↓ (-3.47→-4.88)\", \"A (CIVO)\"]\n          - [008e_v3_s2, Walker, yes, \"↑ (-5.21→-3.83)\", \"B (eval-driven)\"]\n          - [010b, Cheetah, yes, \"↓ (-4.2→-5.1)\", \"A-like\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah_022_s2\", Cheetah, yes, \"flat (-4.5→-4.4)\", \"unclassified\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah_021_s0\", Cheetah, yes, \"↓ then ↑\", \"mixed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy trajectories for all collapsed experiments, colored by environment\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy-based pathway classification 在 Walker Walk 内部有 2/2 clean separation\n      但无法泛化。Cheetah 崩溃 seeds 的 entropy pattern 不落入 A/B 任一类别。\n      这支持 worst 档 narrative：现象是 environment-specific，不是 universal mechanism。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_value_overestimate_mean: \"+45%\"\n      walker_008d_value_overestimate_std: \"22%\"\n      walker_008f_value_calibration_error: \"+8%\"\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_value_overestimate_mean: \"+32%\"\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_value_overestimate_std: \"35%\"\n      distributional_test_p_value_walker: 0.001\n      distributional_test_p_value_cheetah_control: 0.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      Value distribution analysis 在 worst 档下确认：(1) Walker 008d 有显著\n      right-skewed value overestimation（如预期）；(2) Walker 008f calibration 良好；\n      (3) 但 Cheetah no_dt_emb 也有显著 overestimation（+32% mean），\n      尽管 variance 更高。统计检验 p=0.02 对 Cheetah control 仍显著，\n      意味着去掉 dt_emb 在 Cheetah 中不能恢复 value calibration。\n      这是 plan_022 结果的 distributional 确认。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Value calibration summary\"\n        columns: [config, env, \"V(s) - MC_return mean%\", std_pct, \"KS test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008d (trained dt_emb)\", Walker, \"+45%\", \"22%\", 0.001]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", Walker, \"+8%\", \"15%\", 0.34]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", Cheetah, \"+52%\", \"28%\", 0.001]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", Cheetah, \"+32%\", \"35%\", 0.02]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Violin plots: V(s) - MC_return distribution, 4 panels (Walker trained/untrained × Cheetah trained/untrained)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distributional evidence 在 worst 档下强化了核心问题：Cheetah 的\n      no-dt-emb condition 不能恢复 value calibration（p=0.02 仍 significant）。\n      Calibration error +32% 虽然小于 trained dt_emb 的 +52%，但仍足以\n      drive actor exploitation in 2/3 seeds。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors evolution during training\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_initial: 0.85\n      walker_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_35K: 0.42\n      walker_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_55K: 0.28\n      cheetah_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_35K: 0.38\n      cheetah_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_55K: 0.22\n      divergence_rate_walker: -0.012_per_1K\n      divergence_rate_cheetah: -0.014_per_1K\n      cross_env_pattern: similar_divergence\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt_embedding cosine similarity 在两个环境中都快速下降——dt_emb 学会了区分\n      dt=1 和 dt=2。这在两个环境中一致，本身支持 \"dt_emb learns to condition\"\n      的故事。但在 worst 档下，这个 analysis 的问题是：cosine similarity divergence\n      rate 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 中相似，但 outcome 不同（Walker 008f 不崩溃，\n      Cheetah no_dt_emb 崩溃）。所以 dt_emb 的 learning dynamics 不是\n      environment-specific outcome 的 predictor。这使得 cosine similarity\n      只是一个 descriptive metric，不具 diagnostic value。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity evolution\"\n        columns: [env, step, cos_sim_dt1_dt2, CIVO_status]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker, 15K, 0.72, \"not yet\"]\n          - [Walker, 35K, 0.42, \"onset (008d)\"]\n          - [Walker, 55K, 0.28, \"collapse (008d)\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 15K, 0.68, \"not yet\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 35K, 0.38, \"onset\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 55K, 0.22, \"collapse\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cosine similarity curves: Walker and Cheetah overlaid, nearly identical divergence rates\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cosine similarity analysis 在 worst 档下成为 null result — 两个环境中\n      dt_emb 学习速度相似，但 outcome 差异来自 RSSM fidelity 差异，不是 dt_emb 本身。\n      This further supports the reframe: dt_emb is an amplifier, not the root cause.\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Compute classification accuracy at various nve thresholds, 0 GPU cost\"\n    expected_results:\n      threshold_1_3x_accuracy: 0.64\n      threshold_1_5x_accuracy: 0.71\n      threshold_1_7x_accuracy: 0.79\n      threshold_2_0x_accuracy: 0.86\n      auroc_walker_only: 0.92\n      auroc_cross_environment: 0.68\n      optimal_threshold_walker: 1.5\n      optimal_threshold_cheetah: 2.5\n      threshold_stability: environment_dependent\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，NVE threshold 分类在 Walker Walk 内部仍表现良好\n      （AUROC 0.92，1.5× threshold 4/4 on original data），但加入 Cheetah 数据后\n      AUROC 降至 0.68。原因：(1) Cheetah no_dt_emb 的 3/3 seeds 都 exceed 1.5×\n      = 3 false positives（被分类为 \"CIVO\" 但实际是 \"RSSM fidelity gap without dt_emb\"）；\n      (2) 如果加入 008f_s3 (NVE 1.72×) 作为 Walker Walk false positive，\n      则 Walker 内部 accuracy 也降至 5/7 = 71%。最佳 threshold 在环境间不一致\n      （Walker 1.5×, Cheetah 2.5×），使得 NVE threshold 不是 universal diagnostic tool\n      而是 environment-specific calibration。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NVE threshold classification results\"\n        columns: [threshold, walker_accuracy, cheetah_accuracy, combined_accuracy, notes]\n        rows:\n          - [1.3, \"5/7 (71%)\", \"3/6 (50%)\", \"8/13 (62%)\", \"too many FP\"]\n          - [1.5, \"5/7 (71%)\", \"3/6 (50%)\", \"8/13 (62%)\", \"008f_s3 breaks Walker\"]\n          - [1.7, \"6/7 (86%)\", \"4/6 (67%)\", \"10/13 (77%)\", \"borderline\"]\n          - [2.0, \"7/7 (100%)\", \"5/6 (83%)\", \"12/13 (92%)\", \"excludes 008f_s3\"]\n      - title: \"AUROC by scope\"\n        columns: [scope, auroc, 95_pct_CI]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk only (original 4 seeds)\", 1.00, \"[0.75, 1.00]\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk (with 008f_s3)\", 0.92, \"[0.70, 1.00]\"]\n          - [\"Cross-environment (Walker + Cheetah)\", 0.68, \"[0.45, 0.88]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curves: Walker-only (solid, high AUC) vs cross-environment (dashed, poor AUC)\"\n      - \"Threshold sweep plot: accuracy vs threshold value, split by environment\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE threshold 的跨环境泛化失败是 worst 档的核心量化证据。\n      审稿人评价：\"A diagnostic marker that requires environment-specific calibration\n      is not a diagnostic marker — it's a fitted parameter. What does 'NVE>1.5× means\n      CIVO' add over 'model is broken' which you can already see from eval decline?\"\n      论文需要承认 NVE threshold 是 Walker-Walk-calibrated，跨环境需要 re-calibration。\n      这削弱了 methodology paper 的 generality claim。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_peak: 820\n      seed0_eval_500K: 790\n      seed1_eval_peak: 800\n      seed1_eval_500K: 770\n      seed2_eval_peak: 835\n      seed2_eval_500K: 810\n      mean_eval_500K: 790\n      std_eval_500K: 20\n      ve_stable_range: \"0.60-0.70\"\n      baseline_established: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是非 locomotion 任务，DreamerV3 应正常收敛。\n      Baseline 在任何 tier 下都应成功。提供第三个环境的 reference。\n      ve_stable 略低于 Walker/Cheetah（Cartpole reward structure 不同）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cartpole baseline 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_peak, eval_500K, ve_stable]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 820, 790, 0.65]\n          - [1, 800, 770, 0.62]\n          - [2, 835, 810, 0.68]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-seed Cartpole baseline convergence curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole baseline 正常。但在 worst 档下，后续实验（051/052）的结果\n      将进一步支持 \"environment-specific phenomenon\" 叙事。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO collapse in Cartpole Swingup\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_nve_peak: 3.2\n      seed0_collapse: true\n      seed0_eval_105K: 150\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.8\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_eval_105K: 420\n      seed2_nve_peak: 2.5\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 350\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      collapse_rate: \"1/3\"\n      mean_nve_peak: 2.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole 的 CIVO trigger 在 worst 档下仅 1/3 collapse。\n      NVE peaks 1.8-3.2×（低于 Walker 008d 的 4.12× 和 Cheetah 的 8.5×）。\n      Cartpole 的 reward 信号相对 dense（每 step 都有 meaningful reward difference），\n      这使得 RSSM 在 Cartpole 的 reward prediction 质量更高，dt=2 error 更小。\n      结果：trained dt_emb 确实 raises NVE，但 collapse rate 更低且 severity 更弱。\n      Cross-environment pattern：Walker 50% collapse, Cheetah 67%, Cartpole 33%。\n      没有一致的 collapse rate — 完全取决于 environment-specific RSSM fidelity。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cartpole CIVO trigger 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, eval_105K, collapse, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 3.2, 150, yes, \"-81%\"]\n          - [1, 1.8, 420, no, \"-47%\"]\n          - [2, 2.5, 350, no, \"-56%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole NVE trajectories showing lower peak severity than Walker/Cheetah\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 的低 collapse rate (1/3) 和低 NVE peaks 进一步支持\n      \"CIVO severity is environment-specific\" 叙事。审稿人总结：\n      \"Three environments, three different collapse rates (33%, 50%, 67%) —\n      the mechanism's strength is entirely determined by environment properties,\n      not by the dt_emb architecture per se.\"\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control in Cartpole Swingup\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_nve_peak: 1.2\n      seed0_eval_105K: 550\n      seed0_exceeds_1_5x: false\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.9\n      seed1_eval_105K: 620\n      seed1_exceeds_1_5x: false\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.1\n      seed2_eval_105K: 580\n      seed2_exceeds_1_5x: false\n      all_below_1_5x: true\n      causal_control_holds: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole 的 causal control 在 worst 档下 holds（all NVE < 1.5×）。\n      但这并不挽回整体叙事——它仅说明 Cartpole 像 Walker Walk 一样：\n      no dt_emb → no CIVO。问题是 Cheetah 不 follow 这个 pattern。\n      跨环境总结：Walker control holds, Cartpole control holds, Cheetah control fails。\n      审稿人评价：\"2/3 environments support your causal control — but the one that\n      doesn't (Cheetah) is actually the harder, more interesting environment.\n      If your mechanism only works on easy tasks, that's a scope limitation,\n      not a finding.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cartpole dt_embed_dim=0 control\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, eval_105K, exceeds_1.5x, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 1.2, 550, no, \"-30%\"]\n          - [1, 0.9, 620, no, \"-21%\"]\n          - [2, 1.1, 580, no, \"-27%\"]\n      - title: \"Cross-environment causal control summary\"\n        columns: [environment, \"control_holds (0/3 > 1.5×)\", \"environments_with_clean_replication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker Walk, \"YES (0/3)\", 1]\n          - [Cartpole Swingup, \"YES (0/3)\", 1]\n          - [Cheetah Run, \"NO (3/3 > 1.5×)\", 0]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Environment comparison bar chart: control NVE peaks by environment\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/3 environments with clean replication 在 worst 档下不够。\n      Cheetah 是标准 DMC benchmark 且 DreamerV3 论文中有 strong results，\n      reviewer 不会接受 \"it works on Walker and Cartpole but not Cheetah\n      so we scope our claims\" — 因为 Cheetah 不是 outlier，而是 standard task。\n      environments_with_clean_replication = 1（将 Cartpole 视为 \"similar to Walker\"，\n      计为同一类）或 2（如果按字面计数），取决于 reviewer 的 generosity。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty; truncate when exceeding threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 380\n      nve_peak: 1.9\n      nve_105K: 1.4\n      collapse: false\n      vs_baseline: \"-59%\"\n      truncation_rate_dt2: 0.45\n      effective_horizon_mean: 5.8\n      uncertainty_threshold_sensitivity: high\n    result_rationale: >\n      Uncertainty-gated truncation 在 worst 档下\"部分 works\"——防止了 collapse\n      （NVE 未达到灾难性水平），但以大幅牺牲 effective horizon 为代价。\n      45% 的 dt=2 transitions 被截断，effective horizon 从 H=8 降至 5.8，\n      导致 learning signal 不足，eval 仅 380（41% baseline）。\n      审稿人评价：\"Truncation prevents collapse at the cost of making the model\n      useless — you're essentially falling back to dt=1 with extra complexity.\n      This is not a mitigation, it's an admission that dt>1 imagination doesn't work.\"\n      更关键的是：uncertainty threshold 需要 per-environment calibration\n      （与 NVE threshold 同样的问题），且对 threshold 值高度敏感。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Uncertainty truncation pilot results\"\n        columns: [metric, value, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [eval_105K, 380, \"41% baseline — worse than dt=1 config (008e_v3 95%)\"]\n          - [nve_peak, 1.9, \"borderline — still approaches 1.5× danger zone\"]\n          - [truncation_rate, \"45%\", \"nearly half dt=2 steps discarded\"]\n          - [effective_H, 5.8, \"below H=8 target — learning signal loss\"]\n          - [threshold_sensitivity, \"high\", \"±10% threshold change → ±25% eval change\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Eval trajectory with truncation rate overlay: as truncation increases, eval stabilizes but stays low\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_060 在 worst 档下确认了一个 negative insight：uncertainty truncation\n      是一种 overly conservative intervention，牺牲太多 learning signal。\n      它不构成 paper contribution——只是另一个 \"dt>1 不 work\" 的数据点。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC environment for stronger generalization claim\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_mean_500K: 250\n      trained_dt_emb_collapse_rate: \"1/3\"\n      trained_dt_emb_nve_peak_mean: 2.8\n      no_dt_emb_control_nve_peak_mean: 1.9\n      no_dt_emb_exceeds_1_5x: \"2/3\"\n      control_failed: true\n      pattern: \"similar to Cheetah\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是 hard locomotion task（DreamerV3 baseline 在 Hopper 上\n      本身就波动大）。在 worst 档下，Hopper 的结果类似 Cheetah：\n      (1) CIVO trigger works（NVE 2.8× mean, 1/3 collapse）；\n      (2) control fails（no_dt_emb 仍有 2/3 seeds exceed 1.5×）。\n      这进一步确认 \"causal control 仅在 simple/smooth reward environments 成立\"。\n      Hopper 和 Cheetah 的共同特征：reward landscape 更稀疏或更 nonlinear，\n      RSSM fidelity gap at dt=2 更大，dt_emb 不再是 CIVO 的 sole enabler。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Hopper results summary (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [config, collapse_rate, mean_nve_peak, control_holds]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, \"0/3\", 0.7, \"-\"]\n          - [trained_dt_emb, \"1/3\", 2.8, \"-\"]\n          - [no_dt_emb, \"0/3 collapse\", 1.9, \"NO (2/3 > 1.5×)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Hopper learning curves: high variance even in baseline; hard to distinguish signal from noise\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hopper 数据在 worst 档下本身就 noisy（hard task, high variance），\n      使得统计推断更困难。加上 control 失败，Hopper 不增加 paper 的说服力。\n      Final cross-environment tally: 4 environments tested, causal control holds\n      in 2 (Walker, Cartpole), fails in 2 (Cheetah, Hopper)。这是 50/50 —\n      reviewer 不可能接受 \"the mechanism is universal\" with 50% replication。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis (0 GPU)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Classification accuracy at various thresholds across all seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      nve_threshold_classification_accuracy: 0.71\n      auroc_walker: 0.92\n      auroc_all_envs: 0.68\n      optimal_threshold_varies_by_env: true\n      walker_optimal: 1.5\n      cheetah_optimal: 2.5\n      cartpole_optimal: 1.7\n      hopper_optimal: 2.2\n      bootstrap_ci_delta_nve_lower_bound: 0.3\n      bootstrap_exceedance_pct: 72\n    result_rationale: >\n      NVE threshold 在 worst 档下仍有 some discriminative power（AUROC 0.68 > random），\n      但远未达到 \"reliable diagnostic\" 水平。Classification accuracy 71% 意味着\n      ~30% misclassification rate（both FP and FN）。Bootstrap CI lower bound 0.3\n      勉强 >0（方向对），但 exceedance 72% 远低于 95% CI 的 conventional threshold。\n      审稿人评价：\"A diagnostic with 30% error rate and environment-specific thresholds\n      is a starting point for methodology research, not a finished contribution.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment threshold analysis\"\n        columns: [env, optimal_threshold, accuracy_at_1.5x, AUROC, n_datapoints]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker, 1.5, \"5/7 (71%)\", 0.92, 7]\n          - [Cheetah, 2.5, \"5/6 (83%)\", 0.78, 6]\n          - [Cartpole, 1.7, \"5/6 (83%)\", 0.89, 6]\n          - [Hopper, 2.2, \"4/6 (67%)\", 0.72, 6]\n          - [ALL, \"-\", \"19/25 (76%)\", 0.68, 25]\n      - title: \"Bootstrap statistics (all environments)\"\n        columns: [metric, value, CI_95]\n        rows:\n          - [delta_NVE_trained_vs_untrained, 1.8, \"[0.3, 3.2]\"]\n          - [exceedance_pct, \"72%\", \"[55%, 88%]\"]\n          - [classification_accuracy_at_1.5x, \"71%\", \"[55%, 85%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUROC curves by environment + combined\"\n      - \"Bootstrap distribution of Δ NVE with CI overlay\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_034 的 worst 档结果对 methodology contribution 是关键的：\n      NVE monitoring 有 some value（AUROC > random），但 environment-specific\n      calibration requirement 削弱了 \"general diagnostic toolkit\" 的 pitch。\n      CoRL reviewer 需要 \"plug and play\" methodology，不是 \"first calibrate\n      per-environment then use.\" Bootstrap CI includes 0.3 as lower bound\n      (barely positive) — the effect is real but small and unreliable.\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41760,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41760},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f272e0bb-5347-482e-afcd-36240c7eec89","uuid":"fae25215-e9ef-4212-8779-ca582ed8001e"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":357686,"duration_api_ms":359437,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心因果链（trained dt_emb → CIVO → collapse）作为 universal mechanism 不成立——\n  可能是 Walker Walk + RSSM 的特异性现象，而非 imagination-based AC 的通用漏洞。\n  Reframe 方向（仍冲 CoRL）：从 \"mechanism paper\" 转为 \"methodology paper\"——\n  贡献不是 CIVO 本身，而是 factorial diagnosis + NVE monitoring + gradient decomposition 的诊断方法论。\n  关键失败点：Cheetah 控制实验 NVE > 2.0×（跨环境因果控制失败）；008f_s3 NVE > 1.5×（untrained dt_emb 保护被否证）；\n  NVE 1.5× 阈值分类精度 < 75%。35pp decomposition 被 confound with SGS side effects。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse with 2 more seeds (009e seed 1, 009b seed 2)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 55000\n      seed1_eval_final_105K: 131\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 25000\n      seed2_eval_final_105K: 268\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      collapse_rate: 0.5\n      nve_exceeds_1_5x_rate: 1.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据（009e collapsed NVE 4.12×@55K; 009b self-corrected NVE 2.05×→0.38×）。\n      在 worst 档，这些结果本身成立，但 1/2 崩溃率意味着 CIVO 不是确定性的——\n      仅是一个随机事件。当 Cheetah 的 dt_embed_dim=0 控制也出现 NVE>2.0× 时，\n      Walker Walk 的 1/2 崩溃率变得不具说服力：究竟是 trained dt_emb 引起的，\n      还是配置组合的随机脆弱性？审稿人将质疑 n=2 的统计功效。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008d cross-seed comparison\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, nve_peak_step, eval_105K, collapse, mechanism]\n        rows:\n          - [0(=009e), 4.12, 55K, 131, yes, \"value-driven CIVO\"]\n          - [2(=009b), 2.05, 25K, 268, no, \"transient→self-correction\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectory overlay: seed 0 accelerating to 4.12× vs seed 2 transient spike then monotone decline\"\n    analysis: >\n      崩溃率 50% 在 worst 档下不足以支持 mechanism claim——reviewer 会说这是 \"coin flip\"\n      而非 \"reliable trigger\"。NVE>1.5× threshold 在 Walker Walk 内部仍有 4/4 separation，\n      但当 Cheetah 控制实验也出现高 NVE 时，这个 threshold 的跨环境泛化性崩溃。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control stability — 008f_s3 (third seed) 是关键\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009f_status: killed_no_data\n      seed2_009c_eval_105K: 148.34\n      seed2_009c_nve_105K: 1.14\n      seed3_008f_s3_eval_peak: 280\n      seed3_008f_s3_eval_105K: 165\n      seed3_008f_s3_nve_peak: 1.72\n      seed3_008f_s3_nve_peak_step: 85000\n      seed3_exceeds_1_5x: true\n      protection_falsified: true\n      classification_accuracy_post_s3: 0.71\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：008f_s3 NVE > 1.5×。机制：在 dt_embed_dim=0 条件下，\n      RSSM 仍需处理 dt=2 transitions（subsample ON），reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2\n      （reward gap 1.01×），但 observation decoder 的 dt=2 误差累积在某些 seed 下\n      仍可通过 critic 误导 actor。009c 已在 105K 达到 NVE=1.14×（borderline），\n      008f_s3 在更长 run 或不同初始化下跨越 1.5×。这不是经典 CIVO（无 dt_emb amplification），\n      而是 \"raw RSSM fidelity gap\" 本身的有限 value overestimation——但它破坏了\n      NVE 1.5× 作为 trained vs untrained dt_emb 的 perfect separator 的故事。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008f (no dt_emb) all seeds NVE summary\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, nve_peak_step, exceeds_1.5x, eval_105K]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 1.02, 25K, no, 503]\n          - [2(009c), 1.14, 105K, no, 148]\n          - [3(008f_s3), 1.72, 85K, \"YES\", 165]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectory: three 008f seeds overlaid, with 1.5× threshold line — s3 crosses threshold\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f_s3 跨越 NVE 1.5× 是 worst 档的核心打击点。此前 4/4 perfect separation\n      （trained 2/2 exceed, untrained 0/2 exceed）变为 5/7 imperfect separation\n      （trained 2/2+009e+009b=4/4 exceed, untrained 1/3 exceed = 008f_s3）。\n      分类精度从 100% 降至 ~71%（5/7 correct）。审稿人将质疑：如果没有 dt_emb\n      也能出现 NVE>1.5×，那么 trained dt_emb 真的是 \"necessary condition\" 吗？\n      或仅是 \"amplifier\"？这削弱了整个 C2 因果链从 \"necessary and sufficient\" 到 \"risk factor\"。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination mitigation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 869.9\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 137.0\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_mechanism: eval_driven_not_CIVO\n      collapse_rate: 0.5\n      mitigation_reliability: unreliable\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据确认（s1 成功 95% baseline, s2 崩溃 via non-CIVO pathway）。\n      在 worst 档，这个 50% 崩溃率与 008d 的 50% 完全相同——dt=1 imagination\n      作为 mitigation 零效果。更糟的是 s2 的崩溃机制（eval-driven, entropy ↑）\n      与经典 CIVO 不同，被 reviewer 视为 \"ad hoc dual-pathway explanation\"\n      而非 genuine insight。审稿人评价：\"claiming two distinct pathways from n=2\n      per pathway is unfalsifiable post-hoc rationalization.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 cross-seed collapse comparison\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, nve_105K, collapse, pathway, entropy_direction]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 869.9, 0.80, no, \"-\", stable]\n          - [2, 137.0, 3.78, yes, \"Pathway B (eval-driven)\", \"↑ -5.21→-3.83\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-panel: s1 healthy monotone rise vs s2 late-onset collapse with diverging entropy\"\n    analysis: >\n      Dual-pathway 在 worst 档被视为 ad hoc。Reviewer 核心批评：\n      \"Two pathways from two seeds is curve-fitting, not science. Show me 10 seeds\n      with clear bimodal distribution, or this is just noise.\" 50% collapse rate\n      means dt=1 imagination provides zero marginal safety over dt=2 imagination\n      (008d also 50%). The entire C6 story collapses into \"trained dt_emb is bad,\n      and we have no mitigation.\"\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 520\n      seed1_nve_range: [0.55, 0.95]\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_recovery_pattern: single_dip_recovery\n      seed2_eval_105K: 380\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.35\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 75000\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_pattern: slow_decline_after_peak\n      cross_seed_consistency: moderate\n      vs_baseline_mean: -48%\n    result_rationale: >\n      008a 的 \"untrained dt_emb\" 实际是 trained dt_emb unexposed to dt>1 data\n      （subsample OFF = 所有训练数据都是 dt=1）。在 worst 档，seed 间变异大：\n      seed 0 达到 778（85% baseline），但 seed 1/2 可能仅达到 380-520（40-57% baseline）。\n      V-recovery pattern 不稳定复现——有的 seed 单次 dip，有的缓慢下滑。\n      NVE 保持 <1.5× 但绝对性能远低于 baseline，reviewer 质疑：\n      \"suppressed v/e is not suppressed degradation — 008a still loses 48% performance,\n      making it useless as mitigation.\" 这削弱了 C3 从 \"protection\" 到 \"delayed failure\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008a cross-seed summary\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, vs_baseline_pct, nve_peak, collapse, pattern]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 778, \"-15%\", 0.93, no, \"zigzag recovery\"]\n          - [1, 520, \"-43%\", 0.95, no, \"single dip recovery\"]\n          - [2, 380, \"-59%\", 1.35, no, \"slow decline post-peak\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-seed 008a eval curves showing high inter-seed variance; all below baseline but no collapse\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 核心 claim 是 \"untrained dt_emb prevents optimistic drift\" — 这在 worst 档仍成立\n      （NVE < 1.5×），但 practical value 被质疑。平均 -48% vs baseline 意味着\n      \"preventing collapse by preventing learning\" — reviewer 评价：\n      \"You've shown that removing information prevents exploitation, which is trivially true.\"\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"Frozen dt_embedding (requires_grad=False), 诊断 dt_emb TRAINING 是否是必要条件\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 204\n      nve_peak: 0.47\n      nve_105K: 0.42\n      collapse: false\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      mechanism: gradient_starvation\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      comparison_vs_008d: \"no collapse but severe underperformance\"\n      comparison_vs_008f: \"similar non-collapse but different mechanism\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 exp_015b 数据：NVE 0.39-0.47（远低于 1.0，critic 低估），actor_loss→0\n      （gradient starvation），eval 80-238 高波动无稳定收敛。在 worst 档，\n      这个结果被 reviewer 视为 confounding：frozen dt_emb 不崩溃是因为\n      gradient starvation 阻止了所有学习，不是因为 dt_emb training 是 CIVO 的原因。\n      \"You prevented CIVO by preventing learning entirely — this doesn't isolate the mechanism.\"\n      与 008f（dt_embed_dim=0）的区别不清晰：两者都不崩溃，但原因可能完全不同\n      （015b = gradient starvation; 008f = no conditioning information）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Frozen dt_emb vs controls\"\n        columns: [config, eval_105K, nve_peak, mechanism, informative_for_C2]\n        rows:\n          - [\"015b (frozen)\", 204, 0.47, \"gradient starvation\", \"confounded\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained)\", 131, 4.12, \"CIVO\", \"yes (positive control)\"]\n          - [\"008f (dim=0)\", 503, 1.02, \"no conditioning\", \"yes (negative control)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-way comparison: 008d collapse, 008f zigzag recovery, 015b flat low-performance\"\n    analysis: >\n      015b 在 worst 档被视为 uninformative control。Reviewer 评价：\n      \"Freezing the embedding creates a fundamentally different learning regime\n      (gradient starvation in actor) — you cannot conclude that training is the\n      causal factor when your intervention has multiple confounded effects.\"\n      2×2 消融矩阵（trained/frozen × exposed/unexposed）的 frozen row 全部被\n      gradient starvation 污染，无法干净解读。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Narrow true collapse probability of dt=1 imagination config\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_105K: 780\n      seed3_nve_105K: 0.72\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      seed4_eval_105K: 95\n      seed4_nve_peak: 4.2\n      seed4_nve_peak_step: 85000\n      seed4_collapse: true\n      seed4_mechanism: \"mixed — value and eval co-decline\"\n      total_collapse_rate: \"2/4 = 50%\"\n      confidence_interval_collapse_rate: \"[0.15, 0.85] (Clopper-Pearson 95%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下，008e_v3 的崩溃率维持 ~50%（2/4 seeds collapse）。Seed 4 崩溃\n      机制既不完全像 Pathway A（value explosion）也不完全像 Pathway B（eval-driven），\n      而是 \"mixed\" — 进一步削弱 dual-pathway 作为干净分类的可信度。\n      Clopper-Pearson 95% CI for 2/4 = [0.07, 0.93]，统计功效极低。\n      Reviewer 评价：\"50% collapse from n=4 gives CI [0.07, 0.93] — you literally\n      cannot distinguish this from any collapse rate between 7% and 93%.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"008e_v3 all seeds summary\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, nve_105K, collapse, mechanism_classification]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 869.9, 0.80, no, healthy]\n          - [2, 137.0, 3.78, yes, \"Pathway B (eval-driven)\"]\n          - [3, 780, 0.72, no, healthy]\n          - [4, 95, 4.2, yes, \"mixed/ambiguous\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Four-seed overlay showing bimodal outcome: 2 converge ~800+, 2 collapse <150\"\n    analysis: >\n      50% collapse rate with wide CI is statistically uninformative. The existence of\n      a third mechanism pattern (seed 4 \"mixed\") destroys the dual-pathway narrative.\n      Reviewer 核心批评：\"每多一个 seed 就发明一条新 pathway — 这不是 mechanism discovery，\n      是 overfitting to noise.\" CoRL 审稿标准要求 reproducible results，50% collapse\n      from a supposedly safe configuration is unacceptable for a practical recommendation.\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_peak: 850\n      seed0_eval_500K: 820\n      seed1_eval_peak: 790\n      seed1_eval_500K: 760\n      seed2_eval_peak: 810\n      seed2_eval_500K: 780\n      mean_eval_500K: 787\n      std_eval_500K: 30\n      ve_stable_range: \"0.65-0.75\"\n      baseline_established: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Baseline 在任何 tier 下都应成功——这是 vanilla DreamerV3 on Cheetah Run。\n      已有 exp_010a 达到 849.8。Worst 档下 baseline 正常，cross-seed 一致性好，\n      建立了干净的 reference。这不是 failure point；failure 在后续实验。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah baseline 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_peak, eval_500K, ve_stable]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 850, 820, 0.71]\n          - [1, 790, 760, 0.68]\n          - [2, 810, 780, 0.73]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-seed Cheetah baseline learning curves — consistent convergence to 760-820 range\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 正常建立。为后续 CIVO trigger 和 causal control 提供 reference。\n      Cross-seed std ~30 (3.8% of mean) 表明 Cheetah 的 seed sensitivity 低于 Walker Walk。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO collapse in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_nve_peak: 8.5\n      seed0_nve_peak_step: 75000\n      seed0_collapse: true\n      seed0_eval_105K: 85\n      seed1_nve_peak: 5.2\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 65000\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_eval_105K: 120\n      seed2_nve_peak: 3.8\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 55000\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 310\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      collapse_rate: \"2/3\"\n      mean_nve_peak: 5.83\n      cross_env_replication: partial\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 exp_010b 达到 NVE 14.59× 并崩溃。Worst 档下 CIVO trigger 仍部分成功\n      （2/3 collapse），但 peak NVE 范围 3.8-8.5×（低于 Walker Walk 的 009e 4.12×\n      仅作为下限）。关键问题不在 trigger（它 works），而在 control 不 work。\n      NVE 仍 >1.5× in all seeds，确认 trained dt_emb 确实 triggers pathological overestimation。\n      但 severity 和 timing 跨环境不一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah CIVO trigger 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, peak_step, eval_105K, collapse, vs_baseline_105K]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 8.5, 75K, 85, yes, \"-89%\"]\n          - [1, 5.2, 65K, 120, yes, \"-85%\"]\n          - [2, 3.8, 55K, 310, no, \"-60%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectories for 3 Cheetah CIVO seeds, with Walker Walk 008d/009b overlay for comparison\"\n    analysis: >\n      CIVO trigger 在 Cheetah 仍触发高 NVE，但 timing 和 severity 不同于 Walker Walk。\n      这本身不是 worst 档的核心问题——问题在于 control 也出现高 NVE。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"核心跨环境因果控制 — worst 档的关键失败点\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_nve_peak: 2.8\n      seed0_nve_peak_step: 75000\n      seed0_eval_105K: 280\n      seed0_exceeds_1_5x: true\n      seed1_nve_peak: 2.1\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 85000\n      seed1_eval_105K: 350\n      seed1_exceeds_1_5x: true\n      seed2_nve_peak: 3.5\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 65000\n      seed2_eval_105K: 190\n      seed2_exceeds_1_5x: true\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      mean_nve_peak: 2.8\n      all_exceed_1_5x: true\n      causal_control_failed: true\n      cheetah_control_nve_peak: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 worst 档的核心破坏性结果。Cheetah 中去掉 dt_embedding 后 NVE 仍达 2.0-3.5×。\n      机制解释：Cheetah Run 的 reward landscape 比 Walker Walk 更稀疏（locomotion reward\n      与速度线性相关，但 early training 中 reward signal 噪声大），RSSM 在 Cheetah 中\n      即使没有 dt_emb conditioning，dt=2 transitions 的 reward prediction 偏差也足够\n      大，能通过 critic 产生显著 value overestimation。具体来说，Cheetah 的 reward_MAE\n      at dt=2 即使无 dt_emb 也达到 baseline 的 3-5×（不像 Walker Walk 的 008f 的 75×\n      那么极端，但方向相同且 impact 不同）。这意味着 \"dt_embedding is necessary for CIVO\"\n      仅在 Walker Walk 成立——在 Cheetah 中，RSSM fidelity gap at dt=2 本身就足以\n      trigger pathological overestimation without dt_emb amplification。因果链从\n      \"trained dt_emb → CIVO\" 变为 \"RSSM dt=2 error → CIVO（dt_emb amplifies but\n      is not necessary）\"。这是对 C2 核心 claim 的根本否证。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah dt_embed_dim=0 — CONTROL FAILED\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, peak_step, eval_105K, exceeds_1.5x, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 2.8, 75K, 280, \"YES\", no]\n          - [1, 2.1, 85K, 350, \"YES\", no]\n          - [2, 3.5, 65K, 190, \"YES\", yes]\n      - title: \"Cross-environment causal control comparison\"\n        columns: [environment, config, seeds_exceeding_1.5x, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"0/3\", \"control holds\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"no dt_emb\", \"3/3\", \"CONTROL FAILS\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"008d (trained dt_emb)\", \"2/2\", \"CIVO confirmed\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"trained dt_emb\", \"3/3\", \"CIVO confirmed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment NVE comparison: Walker 008f (all <1.5×) vs Cheetah no-dt-emb (all >1.5×)\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: dt_embed_dim=0 NVE vs environment, showing environment-specific behavior\"\n    analysis: >\n      核心灾难：在 Cheetah 中，去掉 dt_embedding 不能阻止 NVE>1.5×。\n      这直接否证了 \"trained dt_emb is necessary for CIVO\" 作为跨环境通用规律。\n      可能的解释：Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 本身更大（不需要 dt_emb 放大），\n      或者 Cheetah 的 reward structure 让 critic 更容易被 dt=2 误差误导。\n      无论哪种解释，都意味着 Walker Walk 的干净 4/4 separation 是 environment-specific artifact。\n      NVE 1.5× threshold 不是 universal diagnostic marker for trained dt_emb —\n      它是 \"RSSM fidelity sufficient for critic exploitation\" 的 marker，\n      而 dt_emb 仅在某些环境中是该条件的必要 amplifier。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 450\n      seed0_nve_peak: 1.6\n      seed0_nve_105K: 1.2\n      seed1_eval_105K: 520\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.4\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.9\n      seed2_eval_105K: 380\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.8\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.5\n      mean_eval_105K: 450\n      vs_baseline_mean: \"-43%\"\n      seeds_exceeding_1_5x: \"2/3\"\n      protection_partial: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah 中仅提供部分保护。\n      由于 Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 更大（见 plan_022 rationale），\n      即使 dt_emb 未暴露于 dt>1 数据，RSSM 本身在处理环境动态时\n      产生的 compounding error 也会推高 value estimates。2/3 seeds 的 NVE\n      触及或超过 1.5×（虽然短暂），与 Walker Walk 008a 的 consistently <1.0×\n      形成鲜明对比。C3 的 \"untrained dt_emb prevents optimistic drift\"\n      在 Cheetah 中不成立 — 再次说明现象的 environment-specificity。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb (no subsample) 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, nve_peak, nve_105K, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 450, 1.6, 1.2, \"-43%\"]\n          - [1, 520, 1.4, 0.9, \"-34%\"]\n          - [2, 380, 1.8, 1.5, \"-52%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 008a-equivalent vs Walker 008a: NVE trajectories showing environment-dependent suppression\"\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst 档，C3 的 value growth suppression 仅在 Walker Walk 干净复现。\n      Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 的保护力度显著减弱。这进一步支持\n      \"Walker Walk + RSSM 特异性\" 叙事 — CIVO 和 anti-CIVO 机制\n      都是 environment-specific 的，没有 universal pattern。\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1\"\n    expected_results:\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_gap: 3.2\n      cheetah_baseline_reward_gap: 2.8\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_obs_gap: 3.8\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_reward_gap: 1.8\n      cheetah_trained_dt_emb_obs_gap: 1.5\n      cheetah_trained_dt_emb_reward_gap: 3.9\n      walker_vs_cheetah_fidelity_pattern: inconsistent\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity pattern 与 Walker Walk 不同。关键差异：\n      (1) Cheetah baseline obs gap (3.2×) > Walker baseline (2.04×) — Cheetah 的\n      RSSM 在 dt=2 预测本身就更差。(2) Cheetah no_dt_emb reward_gap (1.8×)\n      远高于 Walker 008f (1.01×) — 即使没有 dt_emb，Cheetah 的 reward 预测\n      在 dt=2 时仍有显著偏差。这解释了 plan_022 的失败：Walker 008f 的 reward\n      gap 接近 1.0 使 critic 不被误导，但 Cheetah 的 1.8× reward gap 足以\n      trigger value overestimation without dt_emb。RSSM fidelity analysis 揭示\n      核心问题不是 dt_emb training per se，而是 RSSM dt=2 reward prediction quality —\n      dt_emb 仅在 reward gap 本身低时才是关键 amplifier。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment RSSM fidelity comparison\"\n        columns: [env, config, obs_gap, reward_gap, NVE_outcome]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker, baseline, 2.04, 1.56, healthy]\n          - [Walker, \"008d (trained dt_emb)\", 1.30, 2.78, \"CIVO collapse\"]\n          - [Walker, \"008f (no dt_emb)\", 2.75, 1.01, \"no collapse\"]\n          - [Cheetah, baseline, 3.2, 2.8, healthy]\n          - [Cheetah, \"trained dt_emb\", 1.5, 3.9, \"CIVO collapse\"]\n          - [Cheetah, \"no dt_emb\", 3.8, 1.8, \"NVE>2.0× (!)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: reward_gap × obs_gap × collapse outcome, colored by environment\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSSM fidelity analysis 在 worst 档下揭示一个关键 insight：\n      CIVO 的 necessary condition 不是 trained dt_emb，而是 \"sufficient reward\n      prediction error at dt>1 to mislead critic\"。dt_emb 在 Walker Walk 中是\n      这个条件的 sole enabler（008f reward_gap=1.01 without dt_emb），但在 Cheetah\n      中 RSSM 本身的 dt=2 reward error 就足够大（1.8× without dt_emb）。\n      这是 important methodological finding 但破坏了 C2 的 clean causal story。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor_entropy vs training step for healthy vs collapsed configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_entropy_decline_rate: -0.035_per_1K_steps\n      walker_008e_v3_s2_entropy_rise_rate: +0.028_per_1K_steps\n      cheetah_collapsed_entropy_pattern: mixed\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_collapsed_seed2_entropy: declining\n      pathway_classification_consistency: poor\n    result_rationale: >\n      Actor entropy analysis 在 worst 档下进一步混淆 mechanism classification。\n      Walker Walk 有干净的双模式（008d: entropy ↓ = CIVO Pathway A; 008e_v3_s2:\n      entropy ↑ = Pathway B）。但 Cheetah 的 collapsed seeds 不 fit 任何一种模式：\n      有的 entropy declining（像 Pathway A），有的 flat（neither A nor B），\n      有的 oscillating。这使得 \"dual-pathway\" framework 不能泛化到 Cheetah，\n      变成 Walker-Walk-specific phenomenology。审稿人评价：\n      \"The pathway taxonomy is descriptive, not predictive.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Entropy trajectory classification across environments\"\n        columns: [exp, env, collapse, entropy_direction, pathway_assignment]\n        rows:\n          - [008d_s0, Walker, yes, \"↓ (-3.47→-4.88)\", \"A (CIVO)\"]\n          - [008e_v3_s2, Walker, yes, \"↑ (-5.21→-3.83)\", \"B (eval-driven)\"]\n          - [010b, Cheetah, yes, \"↓ (-4.2→-5.1)\", \"A-like\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah_022_s2\", Cheetah, yes, \"flat (-4.5→-4.4)\", \"unclassified\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah_021_s0\", Cheetah, yes, \"↓ then ↑\", \"mixed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy trajectories for all collapsed experiments, colored by environment\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy-based pathway classification 在 Walker Walk 内部有 2/2 clean separation\n      但无法泛化。Cheetah 崩溃 seeds 的 entropy pattern 不落入 A/B 任一类别。\n      这支持 worst 档 narrative：现象是 environment-specific，不是 universal mechanism。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_value_overestimate_mean: \"+45%\"\n      walker_008d_value_overestimate_std: \"22%\"\n      walker_008f_value_calibration_error: \"+8%\"\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_value_overestimate_mean: \"+32%\"\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_value_overestimate_std: \"35%\"\n      distributional_test_p_value_walker: 0.001\n      distributional_test_p_value_cheetah_control: 0.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      Value distribution analysis 在 worst 档下确认：(1) Walker 008d 有显著\n      right-skewed value overestimation（如预期）；(2) Walker 008f calibration 良好；\n      (3) 但 Cheetah no_dt_emb 也有显著 overestimation（+32% mean），\n      尽管 variance 更高。统计检验 p=0.02 对 Cheetah control 仍显著，\n      意味着去掉 dt_emb 在 Cheetah 中不能恢复 value calibration。\n      这是 plan_022 结果的 distributional 确认。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Value calibration summary\"\n        columns: [config, env, \"V(s) - MC_return mean%\", std_pct, \"KS test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008d (trained dt_emb)\", Walker, \"+45%\", \"22%\", 0.001]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", Walker, \"+8%\", \"15%\", 0.34]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", Cheetah, \"+52%\", \"28%\", 0.001]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", Cheetah, \"+32%\", \"35%\", 0.02]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Violin plots: V(s) - MC_return distribution, 4 panels (Walker trained/untrained × Cheetah trained/untrained)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distributional evidence 在 worst 档下强化了核心问题：Cheetah 的\n      no-dt-emb condition 不能恢复 value calibration（p=0.02 仍 significant）。\n      Calibration error +32% 虽然小于 trained dt_emb 的 +52%，但仍足以\n      drive actor exploitation in 2/3 seeds。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors evolution during training\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_initial: 0.85\n      walker_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_35K: 0.42\n      walker_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_55K: 0.28\n      cheetah_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_35K: 0.38\n      cheetah_cosine_sim_dt1_dt2_55K: 0.22\n      divergence_rate_walker: -0.012_per_1K\n      divergence_rate_cheetah: -0.014_per_1K\n      cross_env_pattern: similar_divergence\n    result_rationale: >\n      dt_embedding cosine similarity 在两个环境中都快速下降——dt_emb 学会了区分\n      dt=1 和 dt=2。这在两个环境中一致，本身支持 \"dt_emb learns to condition\"\n      的故事。但在 worst 档下，这个 analysis 的问题是：cosine similarity divergence\n      rate 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 中相似，但 outcome 不同（Walker 008f 不崩溃，\n      Cheetah no_dt_emb 崩溃）。所以 dt_emb 的 learning dynamics 不是\n      environment-specific outcome 的 predictor。这使得 cosine similarity\n      只是一个 descriptive metric，不具 diagnostic value。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity evolution\"\n        columns: [env, step, cos_sim_dt1_dt2, CIVO_status]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker, 15K, 0.72, \"not yet\"]\n          - [Walker, 35K, 0.42, \"onset (008d)\"]\n          - [Walker, 55K, 0.28, \"collapse (008d)\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 15K, 0.68, \"not yet\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 35K, 0.38, \"onset\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 55K, 0.22, \"collapse\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cosine similarity curves: Walker and Cheetah overlaid, nearly identical divergence rates\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cosine similarity analysis 在 worst 档下成为 null result — 两个环境中\n      dt_emb 学习速度相似，但 outcome 差异来自 RSSM fidelity 差异，不是 dt_emb 本身。\n      This further supports the reframe: dt_emb is an amplifier, not the root cause.\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Compute classification accuracy at various nve thresholds, 0 GPU cost\"\n    expected_results:\n      threshold_1_3x_accuracy: 0.64\n      threshold_1_5x_accuracy: 0.71\n      threshold_1_7x_accuracy: 0.79\n      threshold_2_0x_accuracy: 0.86\n      auroc_walker_only: 0.92\n      auroc_cross_environment: 0.68\n      optimal_threshold_walker: 1.5\n      optimal_threshold_cheetah: 2.5\n      threshold_stability: environment_dependent\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，NVE threshold 分类在 Walker Walk 内部仍表现良好\n      （AUROC 0.92，1.5× threshold 4/4 on original data），但加入 Cheetah 数据后\n      AUROC 降至 0.68。原因：(1) Cheetah no_dt_emb 的 3/3 seeds 都 exceed 1.5×\n      = 3 false positives（被分类为 \"CIVO\" 但实际是 \"RSSM fidelity gap without dt_emb\"）；\n      (2) 如果加入 008f_s3 (NVE 1.72×) 作为 Walker Walk false positive，\n      则 Walker 内部 accuracy 也降至 5/7 = 71%。最佳 threshold 在环境间不一致\n      （Walker 1.5×, Cheetah 2.5×），使得 NVE threshold 不是 universal diagnostic tool\n      而是 environment-specific calibration。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NVE threshold classification results\"\n        columns: [threshold, walker_accuracy, cheetah_accuracy, combined_accuracy, notes]\n        rows:\n          - [1.3, \"5/7 (71%)\", \"3/6 (50%)\", \"8/13 (62%)\", \"too many FP\"]\n          - [1.5, \"5/7 (71%)\", \"3/6 (50%)\", \"8/13 (62%)\", \"008f_s3 breaks Walker\"]\n          - [1.7, \"6/7 (86%)\", \"4/6 (67%)\", \"10/13 (77%)\", \"borderline\"]\n          - [2.0, \"7/7 (100%)\", \"5/6 (83%)\", \"12/13 (92%)\", \"excludes 008f_s3\"]\n      - title: \"AUROC by scope\"\n        columns: [scope, auroc, 95_pct_CI]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk only (original 4 seeds)\", 1.00, \"[0.75, 1.00]\"]\n          - [\"Walker Walk (with 008f_s3)\", 0.92, \"[0.70, 1.00]\"]\n          - [\"Cross-environment (Walker + Cheetah)\", 0.68, \"[0.45, 0.88]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curves: Walker-only (solid, high AUC) vs cross-environment (dashed, poor AUC)\"\n      - \"Threshold sweep plot: accuracy vs threshold value, split by environment\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE threshold 的跨环境泛化失败是 worst 档的核心量化证据。\n      审稿人评价：\"A diagnostic marker that requires environment-specific calibration\n      is not a diagnostic marker — it's a fitted parameter. What does 'NVE>1.5× means\n      CIVO' add over 'model is broken' which you can already see from eval decline?\"\n      论文需要承认 NVE threshold 是 Walker-Walk-calibrated，跨环境需要 re-calibration。\n      这削弱了 methodology paper 的 generality claim。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_peak: 820\n      seed0_eval_500K: 790\n      seed1_eval_peak: 800\n      seed1_eval_500K: 770\n      seed2_eval_peak: 835\n      seed2_eval_500K: 810\n      mean_eval_500K: 790\n      std_eval_500K: 20\n      ve_stable_range: \"0.60-0.70\"\n      baseline_established: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是非 locomotion 任务，DreamerV3 应正常收敛。\n      Baseline 在任何 tier 下都应成功。提供第三个环境的 reference。\n      ve_stable 略低于 Walker/Cheetah（Cartpole reward structure 不同）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cartpole baseline 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_peak, eval_500K, ve_stable]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 820, 790, 0.65]\n          - [1, 800, 770, 0.62]\n          - [2, 835, 810, 0.68]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-seed Cartpole baseline convergence curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole baseline 正常。但在 worst 档下，后续实验（051/052）的结果\n      将进一步支持 \"environment-specific phenomenon\" 叙事。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Replicate CIVO collapse in Cartpole Swingup\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_nve_peak: 3.2\n      seed0_collapse: true\n      seed0_eval_105K: 150\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.8\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_eval_105K: 420\n      seed2_nve_peak: 2.5\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 350\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      collapse_rate: \"1/3\"\n      mean_nve_peak: 2.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole 的 CIVO trigger 在 worst 档下仅 1/3 collapse。\n      NVE peaks 1.8-3.2×（低于 Walker 008d 的 4.12× 和 Cheetah 的 8.5×）。\n      Cartpole 的 reward 信号相对 dense（每 step 都有 meaningful reward difference），\n      这使得 RSSM 在 Cartpole 的 reward prediction 质量更高，dt=2 error 更小。\n      结果：trained dt_emb 确实 raises NVE，但 collapse rate 更低且 severity 更弱。\n      Cross-environment pattern：Walker 50% collapse, Cheetah 67%, Cartpole 33%。\n      没有一致的 collapse rate — 完全取决于 environment-specific RSSM fidelity。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cartpole CIVO trigger 3 seeds\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, eval_105K, collapse, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 3.2, 150, yes, \"-81%\"]\n          - [1, 1.8, 420, no, \"-47%\"]\n          - [2, 2.5, 350, no, \"-56%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole NVE trajectories showing lower peak severity than Walker/Cheetah\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 的低 collapse rate (1/3) 和低 NVE peaks 进一步支持\n      \"CIVO severity is environment-specific\" 叙事。审稿人总结：\n      \"Three environments, three different collapse rates (33%, 50%, 67%) —\n      the mechanism's strength is entirely determined by environment properties,\n      not by the dt_emb architecture per se.\"\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control in Cartpole Swingup\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_nve_peak: 1.2\n      seed0_eval_105K: 550\n      seed0_exceeds_1_5x: false\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.9\n      seed1_eval_105K: 620\n      seed1_exceeds_1_5x: false\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.1\n      seed2_eval_105K: 580\n      seed2_exceeds_1_5x: false\n      all_below_1_5x: true\n      causal_control_holds: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole 的 causal control 在 worst 档下 holds（all NVE < 1.5×）。\n      但这并不挽回整体叙事——它仅说明 Cartpole 像 Walker Walk 一样：\n      no dt_emb → no CIVO。问题是 Cheetah 不 follow 这个 pattern。\n      跨环境总结：Walker control holds, Cartpole control holds, Cheetah control fails。\n      审稿人评价：\"2/3 environments support your causal control — but the one that\n      doesn't (Cheetah) is actually the harder, more interesting environment.\n      If your mechanism only works on easy tasks, that's a scope limitation,\n      not a finding.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cartpole dt_embed_dim=0 control\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, eval_105K, exceeds_1.5x, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 1.2, 550, no, \"-30%\"]\n          - [1, 0.9, 620, no, \"-21%\"]\n          - [2, 1.1, 580, no, \"-27%\"]\n      - title: \"Cross-environment causal control summary\"\n        columns: [environment, \"control_holds (0/3 > 1.5×)\", \"environments_with_clean_replication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker Walk, \"YES (0/3)\", 1]\n          - [Cartpole Swingup, \"YES (0/3)\", 1]\n          - [Cheetah Run, \"NO (3/3 > 1.5×)\", 0]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Environment comparison bar chart: control NVE peaks by environment\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/3 environments with clean replication 在 worst 档下不够。\n      Cheetah 是标准 DMC benchmark 且 DreamerV3 论文中有 strong results，\n      reviewer 不会接受 \"it works on Walker and Cartpole but not Cheetah\n      so we scope our claims\" — 因为 Cheetah 不是 outlier，而是 standard task。\n      environments_with_clean_replication = 1（将 Cartpole 视为 \"similar to Walker\"，\n      计为同一类）或 2（如果按字面计数），取决于 reviewer 的 generosity。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty; truncate when exceeding threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 380\n      nve_peak: 1.9\n      nve_105K: 1.4\n      collapse: false\n      vs_baseline: \"-59%\"\n      truncation_rate_dt2: 0.45\n      effective_horizon_mean: 5.8\n      uncertainty_threshold_sensitivity: high\n    result_rationale: >\n      Uncertainty-gated truncation 在 worst 档下\"部分 works\"——防止了 collapse\n      （NVE 未达到灾难性水平），但以大幅牺牲 effective horizon 为代价。\n      45% 的 dt=2 transitions 被截断，effective horizon 从 H=8 降至 5.8，\n      导致 learning signal 不足，eval 仅 380（41% baseline）。\n      审稿人评价：\"Truncation prevents collapse at the cost of making the model\n      useless — you're essentially falling back to dt=1 with extra complexity.\n      This is not a mitigation, it's an admission that dt>1 imagination doesn't work.\"\n      更关键的是：uncertainty threshold 需要 per-environment calibration\n      （与 NVE threshold 同样的问题），且对 threshold 值高度敏感。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Uncertainty truncation pilot results\"\n        columns: [metric, value, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [eval_105K, 380, \"41% baseline — worse than dt=1 config (008e_v3 95%)\"]\n          - [nve_peak, 1.9, \"borderline — still approaches 1.5× danger zone\"]\n          - [truncation_rate, \"45%\", \"nearly half dt=2 steps discarded\"]\n          - [effective_H, 5.8, \"below H=8 target — learning signal loss\"]\n          - [threshold_sensitivity, \"high\", \"±10% threshold change → ±25% eval change\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Eval trajectory with truncation rate overlay: as truncation increases, eval stabilizes but stays low\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_060 在 worst 档下确认了一个 negative insight：uncertainty truncation\n      是一种 overly conservative intervention，牺牲太多 learning signal。\n      它不构成 paper contribution——只是另一个 \"dt>1 不 work\" 的数据点。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC environment for stronger generalization claim\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_mean_500K: 250\n      trained_dt_emb_collapse_rate: \"1/3\"\n      trained_dt_emb_nve_peak_mean: 2.8\n      no_dt_emb_control_nve_peak_mean: 1.9\n      no_dt_emb_exceeds_1_5x: \"2/3\"\n      control_failed: true\n      pattern: \"similar to Cheetah\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 是 hard locomotion task（DreamerV3 baseline 在 Hopper 上\n      本身就波动大）。在 worst 档下，Hopper 的结果类似 Cheetah：\n      (1) CIVO trigger works（NVE 2.8× mean, 1/3 collapse）；\n      (2) control fails（no_dt_emb 仍有 2/3 seeds exceed 1.5×）。\n      这进一步确认 \"causal control 仅在 simple/smooth reward environments 成立\"。\n      Hopper 和 Cheetah 的共同特征：reward landscape 更稀疏或更 nonlinear，\n      RSSM fidelity gap at dt=2 更大，dt_emb 不再是 CIVO 的 sole enabler。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Hopper results summary (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [config, collapse_rate, mean_nve_peak, control_holds]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, \"0/3\", 0.7, \"-\"]\n          - [trained_dt_emb, \"1/3\", 2.8, \"-\"]\n          - [no_dt_emb, \"0/3 collapse\", 1.9, \"NO (2/3 > 1.5×)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Hopper learning curves: high variance even in baseline; hard to distinguish signal from noise\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hopper 数据在 worst 档下本身就 noisy（hard task, high variance），\n      使得统计推断更困难。加上 control 失败，Hopper 不增加 paper 的说服力。\n      Final cross-environment tally: 4 environments tested, causal control holds\n      in 2 (Walker, Cartpole), fails in 2 (Cheetah, Hopper)。这是 50/50 —\n      reviewer 不可能接受 \"the mechanism is universal\" with 50% replication。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis (0 GPU)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Classification accuracy at various thresholds across all seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      nve_threshold_classification_accuracy: 0.71\n      auroc_walker: 0.92\n      auroc_all_envs: 0.68\n      optimal_threshold_varies_by_env: true\n      walker_optimal: 1.5\n      cheetah_optimal: 2.5\n      cartpole_optimal: 1.7\n      hopper_optimal: 2.2\n      bootstrap_ci_delta_nve_lower_bound: 0.3\n      bootstrap_exceedance_pct: 72\n    result_rationale: >\n      NVE threshold 在 worst 档下仍有 some discriminative power（AUROC 0.68 > random），\n      但远未达到 \"reliable diagnostic\" 水平。Classification accuracy 71% 意味着\n      ~30% misclassification rate（both FP and FN）。Bootstrap CI lower bound 0.3\n      勉强 >0（方向对），但 exceedance 72% 远低于 95% CI 的 conventional threshold。\n      审稿人评价：\"A diagnostic with 30% error rate and environment-specific thresholds\n      is a starting point for methodology research, not a finished contribution.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-environment threshold analysis\"\n        columns: [env, optimal_threshold, accuracy_at_1.5x, AUROC, n_datapoints]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker, 1.5, \"5/7 (71%)\", 0.92, 7]\n          - [Cheetah, 2.5, \"5/6 (83%)\", 0.78, 6]\n          - [Cartpole, 1.7, \"5/6 (83%)\", 0.89, 6]\n          - [Hopper, 2.2, \"4/6 (67%)\", 0.72, 6]\n          - [ALL, \"-\", \"19/25 (76%)\", 0.68, 25]\n      - title: \"Bootstrap statistics (all environments)\"\n        columns: [metric, value, CI_95]\n        rows:\n          - [delta_NVE_trained_vs_untrained, 1.8, \"[0.3, 3.2]\"]\n          - [exceedance_pct, \"72%\", \"[55%, 88%]\"]\n          - [classification_accuracy_at_1.5x, \"71%\", \"[55%, 85%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUROC curves by environment + combined\"\n      - \"Bootstrap distribution of Δ NVE with CI overlay\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_034 的 worst 档结果对 methodology contribution 是关键的：\n      NVE monitoring 有 some value（AUROC > random），但 environment-specific\n      calibration requirement 削弱了 \"general diagnostic toolkit\" 的 pitch。\n      CoRL reviewer 需要 \"plug and play\" methodology，不是 \"first calibrate\n      per-environment then use.\" Bootstrap CI includes 0.3 as lower bound\n      (barely positive) — the effect is real but small and unreliable.\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f272e0bb-5347-482e-afcd-36240c7eec89","total_cost_usd":0.7757255000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41760,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":18878,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41760,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18878,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41760},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":36720,"outputTokens":25,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.036845,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18878,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41760,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7388805,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_